    {
      "id": "da1316a7de814a6db6d296138df1ffed",
      "title": "Three lines are not a capacity validation.",
      "summary": null,
      "order": 5,
      "blocks": [
        {
          "id": "232884b498844c47ab47db1c5bf7653b",
          "block_type": "corporate_section",
          "title": null,
          "components": [
            {
              "id": "dd0fe66444304fa78fc4ed988e378570",
              "component_kind": "text",
              "title": null,
              "body": "Strapping sufficiency must be proven against p95 demand and actual mix, including corner-board placement, double straps, changeovers, rejects and availability. The working hypothesis is to assess a fourth line or replace current technology with automatic strappers and automatic corner-board insertion.",
              "items": [],
              "props": {},
              "asset_ids": [],
              "style_tokens": [],
              "evidence_ids": [],
              "knowledge_keys": [],
              "semantic_labels": [],
              "confidence": 1.0
            },
            {
              "id": "75accc217b9b496c82c3112514f47e28",
              "component_kind": "technical_specification",
              "title": null,
              "body": "Required strappers = ceiling[p95 load demand/min ÷ (sustainable capacity per strapper × availability)] + required redundancy",
              "items": [],
              "props": {},
              "asset_ids": [],
              "style_tokens": [],
              "evidence_ids": [],
              "knowledge_keys": [],
              "semantic_labels": [],
              "confidence": 1.0
            },
            {
              "id": "8929cc2795764062aaf8805a5e09560e",
              "component_kind": "text",
              "title": "3 lines challenged",
              "body": "Operating experience indicates insufficient capacity. This must be documented through queues, blocked time, utilization and failure recovery.",
              "items": [],
              "props": {},
              "asset_ids": [],
              "style_tokens": [],
              "evidence_ids": [],
              "knowledge_keys": [],
              "semantic_labels": [],
              "confidence": 1.0
            },
            {
              "id": "e39ffac811a744719d422763517b5000",
              "component_kind": "text",
              "title": "Fourth strapper",
              "body": "Adds capacity and redundancy if routing, space, labor and pickup can distribute the load.",
              "items": [],
              "props": {},
              "asset_ids": [],
              "style_tokens": [],
              "evidence_ids": [],
              "knowledge_keys": [],
              "semantic_labels": [],
              "confidence": 1.0
            },
            {
              "id": "003fd952a0ad4731bae0721a66a88c69",
              "component_kind": "text",
              "title": "Automatic + corner boards",
              "body": "Removes manual tasks from the critical cycle and can sharply increase the final station's sustainable rate.",
              "items": [],
              "props": {},
              "asset_ids": [],
              "style_tokens": [],
              "evidence_ids": [],
              "knowledge_keys": [],
              "semantic_labels": [],
              "confidence": 1.0
            },
            {
              "id": "5ec447e3326945d7bcb9001b4804b194",
              "component_kind": "executive_summary",
              "title": null,
              "body": "Correct interpretation of 400-600% A net 400-600% improvement means the new station would produce 5 to 7 times baseline output if “improvement” is incremental. The audit will define the convention, time current and automatic cycles by SKU, and prevent a commercial claim from becoming a guarantee without FAT/SAT.",
              "items": [],
              "props": {},
              "asset_ids": [],
              "style_tokens": [],
              "evidence_ids": [],
              "knowledge_keys": [],
              "semantic_labels": [],
              "confidence": 1.0
